-- The n-th match stops the walk, so the condition never sees the chunks
-- after it, while `last` and `every` test every chunk (ADR 0074).
on nth
 return [the first item of [4, 2, 0] whose 8 / it > 1, the second item of [4, 2, 0] whose 8 / it > 1, the third item of [5, 6, 7, 8] whose it > 4, the tenth item of (1..20) whose it mod 2 = 0]
end nth

on lastMatch
 return the last item of [4, 2, 0] whose 8 / it > 1
end lastMatch
